  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "go-acyclic-imports",
      "text": "Go forbids import cycles, so 2.2.2 and 2.2.4 always score 10; read hierarchy problems from subsystem cycles and 2.1.x instead.",
      "source": "mmi.md §4"
    },
    {
      "id": "type-granularity",
      "text": "A Go package-level named type stands in for the dissertation's class; the MMI's class thresholds were calibrated on Java, C# and PHP.",
      "source": "mmi.md §3"
    },
    {
      "id": "loc",
      "text": "A line of code is a line on which a token other than a comment starts; test files and generated files are left out of every measure.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "statements",
      "text": "Number of Statements counts every statement except blocks, labels, empty statements and case clauses, including a for loop's init and post.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "cognitive",
      "text": "Cognitive complexity is github.com/uudashr/gocognit's SonarSource count; a function above 15 is a cognitive-complexity warning.",
      "source": "SonarSource, Cognitive Complexity (2017)"
    },
    {
      "id": "complexity-variant",
      "text": "Criterion 1.3.4 uses the modified cyclomatic complexity, above 15.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.3; von Zitzewitz"
    },
    {
      "id": "thresholds",
      "text": "large type > 400 lines, large function > 60 lines, large package > 40 types, largest tolerable type cycle group 5, large file > 800 lines, deepest nesting 4: borrowed guidance, not the chapter's.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "denominators",
      "text": "1.2.1, 2.1.1, 2.1.2 and 3.2 divide violating imports or references by all candidates between different groups; the chapter gives no denominators.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.2"
    },
    {
      "id": "communities",
      "text": "Communities are gonum's Louvain communities (resolution 1, a fixed seed) of the package graph taken as undirected, an edge weighing the imports either way, each split into its connected parts. A package of a subsystem with other packages is misplaced when another subsystem holds more of its community than its own. They are advice and never gate.",
      "source": "IMPROVEMENTS.md 9.3; codetospec internal/communities"
    },
    {
      "id": "static-binding",
      "text": "Dependencies are the imports and references go/types resolves in the build the report reads, for its platform and tags; reflection, dispatch by string and struct tags are not followed. The imports of files the build constraints exclude are read from their source and checked by the import rules alone: forbidden imports, isolations, and fitness's layer access, strict layers, onion, dependents and libraries; graphs, cycles, fan-out and metrics measure the build.",
      "source": "go/types; techne RFC-0002"
    },
    {
      "id": "largest-cycle",
      "text": "Criteria 2.2.3 and 2.2.4 use the largest cycle group.",
      "source": "mmi.md §4"
    },
    {
      "id": "mmi-aggregation",
      "text": "MMI = Σ weight(group) × mean(scores); unscored criteria count 0 toward the low bound and 10 toward the high bound.",
      "source": "mmi.md §2"
    },
    {
      "id": "lcom4",
      "text": "LCOM4 links methods to the fields and methods they select through the receiver; a field no method uses is left out.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.5"
    },
    {
      "id": "decoupling-level",
      "text": "Decoupling Level (Mo et al., ICSE 2016) is not computed: US patent 11,422,800 covers its algorithm.",
      "source": "mmi-ref.md A.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "martin",
      "text": "Martin's metrics count in-scope imports only; abstractness is the share of named types that are interfaces, and instability is 0 for an isolated package.",
      "source": "mmi-ref.md A.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "component-rank",
      "text": "Component Rank is PageRank over type dependencies with damping 0.8, run for a fixed 50 iterations; types that depend on nothing spread their rank evenly.",
      "source": "mmi-ref.md A.1; von Zitzewitz"
    },
    {
      "id": "sdi-cut",
      "text": "SDI cuts are exact for cycle groups of up to 12 elements and use the Eades–Lin–Smyth ordering above that; Coupling.CutMethod says which.",
      "source": "mmi.md §7.5"
    }
  ]
